    "linkedin:b9cd94778a746550bcd91aba": {
      "job": {
        "title": "Backend Engineer (Node.js, TypeScript)",
        "company": "Wiraa",
        "location": "",
        "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/jobs/view/4482075216",
        "platform": "Linkedin",
        "date_posted": "2026-10-21T00:00:00+00:00",
        "is_remote": true,
        "description": "**About The Company**\n Small businesses constitute 99\\.9% of all companies, yet they often face challenges when it comes to communication infrastructure. Many are forced to choose between outdated enterprise phone systems or relying on personal mobile devices, which hampers growth and efficiency. Recognizing this gap, Quo has positioned itself as a transformative force in the communication technology landscape. We are committed to revolutionizing how small businesses connect with their customers by integrating calls, texts, and customer information into a single, easy\\-to\\-use, AI\\-powered platform. Our innovative approach not only simplifies communication but also sets new standards for customer engagement and operational efficiency.\n   \n\n  \n\n Founded with a mission to empower underserved small businesses, Quo has rapidly gained trust, serving over 120,000 companies and earning the \\#1 spot in customer satisfaction on G2\\. Backed by prominent investors such as Y Combinator, Tiger Global, Craft Ventures, and Slow Ventures, we are poised for continued growth and innovation. Our core values emphasize moving quickly, building with determination, and obsessing over delivering tangible value to our users. As a remote\\-first company, we foster a culture of trust, autonomy, and action, dedicated to building inclusive and diverse teams that thrive in a dynamic environment.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n Our AI Agent Platform team is at the forefront of developing Quo’s customer\\-facing AI agents, including Sona, our AI assistant for calls and texts, and Quo Agent, our newly launched workspace agent. This role is critical as the agents are already live with customers, and the challenges ahead involve scaling, enhancing capabilities, and improving reliability. As a Staff Software Engineer, you will serve as the technical lead for this team, responsible for defining and executing the architectural vision that underpins our agent platform.\n   \n\n  \n\n You will have a direct impact on how AI\\-driven interactions are experienced by our customers and how other teams leverage our platform for their own product development. Your work will involve designing complex orchestration systems, memory and self\\-learning features, and ensuring the platform’s performance, reliability, and cost\\-effectiveness grow in tandem with our user base. You will mentor engineers, advocate for best practices, and stay engaged with the latest advancements in large language models (LLMs) and agent tooling to inform our product roadmap.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n* Proven experience in building and scaling backend systems for high\\-traffic products\n* Hands\\-on experience deploying LLM\\-powered systems, especially agent platforms or orchestration layers\n* Strong proficiency in TypeScript and Node.js, or fluency in other backend languages such as Python, Java, or Go\n* Experience with microservices architecture, event\\-driven systems, and workflow engines like Temporal or similar\n* Familiarity with cloud infrastructure, preferably AWS, and container orchestration with Kubernetes\n* Knowledge of databases such as Postgres, MongoDB, Elasticsearch, and caching systems like Redis\n* Understanding of observability tools including Datadog or equivalent for monitoring and troubleshooting\n* Excellent communication skills, with the ability to write clear design documents and explain technical trade\\-offs\n* High level of ownership, initiative, and ability to work independently in a remote environment\n* Passion for AI, machine learning, and staying current with industry developments\n\n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Define and own the architecture of Quo’s AI agent platform, including creation, deployment, and execution layers\n* Develop advanced orchestration capabilities, enabling complex multi\\-agent workflows and long\\-running tasks\n* Design and implement memory and self\\-learning features to improve agent performance over time\n* Ensure the platform’s scalability, performance, reliability, and cost\\-efficiency as usage expands\n* Build developer\\-friendly tools, documentation, and defaults to facilitate cross\\-team adoption and innovation\n* Mentor and review work of engineering team members, fostering a culture of technical excellence\n* Stay informed on latest AI and LLM advancements, translating insights into actionable product strategies\n* Collaborate closely with cross\\-functional teams to align platform development with business goals\n* Participate in technical discussions, design reviews, and hands\\-on coding to drive platform evolution\n\n\n**Benefits**\n* Competitive annual salary, commensurate with experience and skills\n* Equity options aligned with company growth\n* Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage\n* Monthly lifestyle stipend to support well\\-being and productivity\n* Flexible PTO policy to promote work\\-life balance\n* Remote\\-first work environment with opportunities to connect in hub cities\n* Professional development opportunities and a dynamic, innovative team culture\n\n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n Quo is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. We do not discriminate based on race, religion, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability, or any other protected characteristic. We believe that diverse perspectives and experiences drive innovation and success, and we welcome applicants from all backgrounds to join our team.",
